00:09:04.343 --> 00:09:05.878
I don't have Twitter.

00:09:05.878 --> 00:09:07.513
Like, it's, you know, it's
Tucker Carlson on Twitter,

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:09.048
but like, it's not, you know,

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:11.484
I'm not the one checking it
and tweeting this stuff and

00:09:11.484 --> 00:09:14.754 align:start size:97% position:3%
that keeps you kind of
insulated and safe and sane.

00:09:14.754 --> 00:09:17.523
- Yeah, and I have a
huge number of people

00:09:17.523 --> 00:09:18.791
I talk to every day.

00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:20.459
I mean, I spend my whole
life talking to people,

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:21.794
mostly by text,

00:09:21.794 --> 00:09:23.129
but hundreds of people.

00:09:23.129 --> 00:09:24.764
And I try to clear
my text every night,

00:09:24.764 --> 00:09:26.265 align:start size:81% position:19%
it was up until
two in the morning

00:09:26.265 --> 00:09:29.201
in front of the fire,
where I live it's cold,

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:31.637
on September 1st
and with my dogs,

00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:32.872
you know, and I'm up really late

00:09:32.872 --> 00:09:34.640 align:start size:84% position:16%
banging out these
texts, taking notes.

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:37.109
So I speak to a ton of people,

00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:38.411
and not just people in my world,

00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:39.879
not just famous rich people,

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:42.148
but like a lot of random people.

00:09:42.148 --> 00:09:44.483
A waitress that
I had in Big Sur,

00:09:44.483 --> 00:09:47.186
I hope she's watching this,
I know she's a fan of yours,

00:09:47.186 --> 00:09:48.321
years ago,

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:51.223 line:0%
I gave her my text
for some reason,

00:09:51.223 --> 00:09:53.192 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
she and her husband are
like such thoughtful people.

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:55.061 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
And she has been
texting me ever since.

00:09:55.061 --> 00:09:56.596
And I swear, once a month,

00:09:56.596 --> 00:09:59.532
two nights ago, I used one
of her lines on the air.

00:09:59.532 --> 00:10:00.866
Like, at least once a month,

00:10:00.866 --> 00:10:02.602
I'll like run with this
story idea she sends me.

00:10:02.602 --> 00:10:05.805 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I have a huge number of
people that I correspond with,

00:10:05.805 --> 00:10:08.307 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I don't want to
open it up to the mob.

00:10:08.307 --> 00:10:10.242
I mean, 'cause then I
can't think clearly.

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:12.011
And my whole job is,

00:10:12.011 --> 00:10:13.412
you know, and I don't
always pull it off,

00:10:13.412 --> 00:10:15.114
but I really try
to think clearly,

00:10:15.114 --> 00:10:16.616
like what is going on here?

00:10:16.616 --> 00:10:19.051
You know, ascend a little
bit, get higher, look down,

00:10:19.051 --> 00:10:20.553
what are the outlines of this?

00:10:20.553 --> 00:10:23.756 align:start size:97% position:3%
And being involved in this,
fuck you, fuck you too.

00:10:23.756 --> 00:10:24.924
You know, whoa,

00:10:26.092 --> 00:10:28.527
I don't like noise
in my personal life.

00:10:28.527 --> 00:10:30.029
I like quiet,

00:10:30.029 --> 00:10:32.365
and I don't like noise in my
work or intellectual life.

00:10:32.365 --> 00:10:35.468
You know, I like to
think I like nature.

00:10:35.468 --> 00:10:37.370
You know, I like like
hunting and fishing,

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:38.871
I like to be outside,

00:10:38.871 --> 00:10:41.574
I don't want to sit
in a room and read

00:10:41.574 --> 00:10:43.376
other people's hysteria.

00:10:43.376 --> 00:10:45.778
I don't think there's any
upside to that at all.

00:10:45.778 --> 00:10:47.313
- Trust me, man,

00:10:47.313 --> 00:10:48.681
as a guy that just spent
30 days in a rain forest,

00:10:48.681 --> 00:10:50.516 align:start size:84% position:16%
basically, I
completely feel that,

00:10:50.516 --> 00:10:51.784
and I've realized that

00:10:51.784 --> 00:10:53.319
my relationship
with social media

00:10:53.319 --> 00:10:54.387 align:start size:81% position:19%
has to be a little
bit different.

00:10:54.387 --> 00:10:56.055
And one of the last things

00:10:56.055 --> 00:10:58.491 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I remember
before leaving in July

00:10:58.491 --> 00:11:00.192
was that you sorta got accosted

00:11:00.192 --> 00:11:02.261 align:start size:84% position:16%
while you were going
fishing basically

00:11:02.261 --> 00:11:03.696
by some guy.

00:11:03.696 --> 00:11:05.297 align:start size:84% position:16%
And what was so
interesting about it,

00:11:05.297 --> 00:11:06.899
and I say this about
everything these days,

00:11:06.899 --> 00:11:09.201
it's not the incident itself,

00:11:09.201 --> 00:11:10.436
it's not the incident,

00:11:10.436 --> 00:11:12.905
it's the way the media
reacts to the incident.

00:11:12.905 --> 00:11:14.940
So this guy is kind of
getting in your face,

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.542 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the way the
whole media was like,

00:11:16.542 --> 00:11:18.177
yeah, yeah, well,
Tucker is mean,

00:11:18.177 --> 00:11:20.746
so everyone should get in his
face and be more mean about,

00:11:20.746 --> 00:11:22.014
and it's like, man,

00:11:22.014 --> 00:11:24.684
that will lead us all
to a very dark place.

00:11:24.684 --> 00:11:25.951
- Well, someone's
going to get shot.

00:11:25.951 --> 00:11:27.787
I mean, I'm serious.

00:11:27.787 --> 00:11:30.456
I mean like where do
you think that ends,

00:11:30.456 --> 00:11:33.259
you physically confront people

00:11:33.259 --> 00:11:36.595 align:start size:97% position:3%
because you don't like their
opinions about politics

00:11:36.595 --> 00:11:37.830
in front of their children.

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.065
I mean, one of my
kids was there.

00:11:39.065 --> 00:11:41.200 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was in a fly shop
that I've gone to for,

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:42.735
you know, many, many years

00:11:42.735 --> 00:11:44.403 align:start size:84% position:16%
in a town that I've
gone to for many years

00:11:44.403 --> 00:11:46.005
and that I really love.

00:11:46.005 --> 00:11:47.506
And it, gosh, it felt,

00:11:47.506 --> 00:11:50.676
I mean, this is so whiny
and I try never to whine

00:11:50.676 --> 00:11:51.977
in public or private,

00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:53.846
but oh wow, it really
felt like a violation,

00:11:53.846 --> 00:11:55.114
and I thought, well,

00:11:55.114 --> 00:11:56.649
you know, I'm never
going here again,

00:11:56.649 --> 00:11:58.184
which was sad,

00:11:58.184 --> 00:12:00.820
but then, you know, there are
other places to go, I guess.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
I live in a really
beautiful place with just,

00:12:03.522 --> 00:12:06.459
I mean, untold miles of

00:12:06.459 --> 00:12:08.594
empty rivers and
streams and lakes

00:12:08.594 --> 00:12:10.596
and like, why am I
in Montana anyway.

00:12:11.864 --> 00:12:14.033
I'll stay in Maine, you know?

00:12:14.033 --> 00:12:15.901
But anyway, it just
made me sad and,

00:12:15.901 --> 00:12:18.704
but I also think it's
very unwise to do that.

00:12:18.704 --> 00:12:20.372
I lived in DC for 35 years.

00:12:20.372 --> 00:12:23.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would see people all
the time I disagreed with.

00:12:23.042 --> 00:12:25.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I've had
dinner with Nancy Pelosi,

00:12:25.177 --> 00:12:27.179
I stood next to Barney Frank,

00:12:27.179 --> 00:12:28.581
I remember it at an event,

00:12:28.581 --> 00:12:31.050 align:start size:88% position:13%
I could, you know,
that was my whole life.

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:33.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the idea of screaming
at someone because

00:12:33.819 --> 00:12:35.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
that person disagrees
with you was like insane.

00:12:35.621 --> 00:12:37.890
And this is what happens when

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:40.025
you have a secular
society at scale,

00:12:40.025 --> 00:12:42.261 align:start size:88% position:13%
which has never happened
in human history.

00:12:42.261 --> 00:12:44.029
There's always a religion

00:12:44.029 --> 00:12:46.031
because people have
a need for meaning.

00:12:46.031 --> 00:12:47.533
You take that away

00:12:47.533 --> 00:12:49.602
and people just replace it
with political ideology,

00:12:49.602 --> 00:12:51.103 align:start size:81% position:19%
and that's what
it's really about.

00:12:51.103 --> 00:12:54.440 align:start size:97% position:3%
The guy screaming at me
felt that I was an apostate.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.475
You know, I was attacking the
one true faith or something.

00:12:56.475 --> 00:12:58.077
That's not how I see it,

00:12:58.077 --> 00:13:00.746
but it's how a lot
of people do see it,

00:13:00.746 --> 00:13:02.982
and I think that
we should be aware

00:13:02.982 --> 00:13:06.085
that the end point
of this is violence.

00:13:06.085 --> 00:13:07.520
Like, that's where it's going.

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:08.521
You know what I mean?

00:13:08.521 --> 00:13:10.422
And I hate that,
I hate violence,

00:13:10.422 --> 00:13:12.391
I've seen it a lot, actually,

00:13:12.391 --> 00:13:14.059
I'm totally opposed to it.

00:13:14.059 --> 00:13:17.429 align:start size:88% position:13%
But the way that the
things have been set up,

00:13:17.429 --> 00:13:18.798
the way we communicate,

00:13:18.798 --> 00:13:20.132
the end point is violence.

00:13:20.132 --> 00:13:22.902
And I just, I say that
all the time on the air,

00:13:22.902 --> 00:13:24.537 align:start size:84% position:16%
because I think people
should know that,

00:13:24.537 --> 00:13:26.806
let's pull back a little bit.

00:13:26.806 --> 00:13:28.374
- Yeah, which is so
interesting because

00:13:28.374 --> 00:13:29.508
then the way they'll frame it

00:13:29.508 --> 00:13:31.010 align:start size:88% position:13%
is that you're throwing
these firebombs

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:32.411
and it's actually the reverse,

00:13:32.411 --> 00:13:33.679
it's a warning.

00:13:33.679 --> 00:13:36.115
But to your point on
the secularism part,

00:13:36.115 --> 00:13:38.150
do you see where
we're at right now

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:41.120 align:start size:84% position:16%
as just sort of
the end of a purely

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.055
sort of secular America, that

00:13:43.055 --> 00:13:46.826
at the end of just
a secular America,

00:13:46.826 --> 00:13:48.828
two plus two now equals five,

00:13:48.828 --> 00:13:51.831
boys or girls, we don't
know which way is up,

00:13:51.831 --> 00:13:53.632
our history is no
longer our history.

00:13:53.632 --> 00:13:58.504 align:start size:97% position:3%
That sort of without some sort
of undergirding of religion

00:13:58.504 --> 00:14:01.941
or some subset of belief
that this is what you get.

00:14:01.941 --> 00:14:04.343
And I really fear this
because as you know,

00:14:04.343 --> 00:14:06.645
as someone that considered
myself liberal my whole life,

00:14:06.645 --> 00:14:08.614
I wanted that thing to work,

00:14:08.614 --> 00:14:10.316 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I have come to the
uncomfortable truth

00:14:10.316 --> 00:14:13.586
that it cannot work,
it simply cannot work

00:14:13.586 --> 00:14:15.087
when it's purely secular.

00:14:15.087 --> 00:14:17.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, you're always
gonna have a religion and,

00:14:17.389 --> 00:14:19.124
you know, you can say, well,

00:14:19.124 --> 00:14:21.627
the crucifixion is kind
of a ridiculous story,

00:14:21.627 --> 00:14:24.330
the Talmud is sort
of absurd, okay,

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:25.564
but compared to what.

00:14:25.564 --> 00:14:26.999
You know what I mean?

00:14:26.999 --> 00:14:28.767
- Right, what do you
got that's better?

00:14:28.767 --> 00:14:30.236
- Compared to the idea that

00:14:30.236 --> 00:14:32.504 align:start position:0%
men can get pregnant or two
plus two equals five, like it's,

00:14:32.504 --> 00:14:36.242 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, you're trading one
superstition for another,

00:14:36.242 --> 00:14:38.544
and that's just
the state of man.

00:14:38.544 --> 00:14:40.045
Like, we're always gonna have

00:14:40.045 --> 00:14:43.349
a belief in the transcendent
because we're wired that way,

00:14:43.349 --> 00:14:45.150 align:start size:84% position:16%
but you needed to
think carefully about

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:47.386
what god you worship,

00:14:47.386 --> 00:14:50.823
you know, what religion
you sign up for here.

00:14:50.823 --> 00:14:52.825
And I think we should
be honest about it.

00:14:52.825 --> 00:14:55.027
I mean, the political discourse

00:14:55.027 --> 00:14:56.528 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I just
described in that you

00:14:56.528 --> 00:14:58.964
live in the middle
of every single day

00:14:58.964 --> 00:15:01.600
is not about convincing people,

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:04.203
it's not rational
people bringing,

00:15:04.203 --> 00:15:06.338 align:start size:88% position:13%
you know, a set of facts
to the conversation

00:15:06.338 --> 00:15:08.507
to try to persuade the
other side to join them.

00:15:08.507 --> 00:15:09.909
Of course not, it's
a religious war,

00:15:09.909 --> 00:15:11.176
that's exactly what it is.

00:15:11.176 --> 00:15:12.678
So we should just,
we should name it,

00:15:12.678 --> 00:15:15.547
this is a cult, the mask stuff.

00:15:15.547 --> 00:15:17.683
You know, I won't
be boring about it,

00:15:17.683 --> 00:15:19.652
but in one sentence,
like we spent a year.

00:15:19.652 --> 00:15:21.153
First of all,

00:15:21.153 --> 00:15:22.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was really worried about
COVID at the beginning.

00:15:22.388 --> 00:15:23.989 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think we were the
first show on cable TV

00:15:23.989 --> 00:15:26.091 align:start size:81% position:19%
to note that COVID
existed 'cause

00:15:26.091 --> 00:15:28.127
we're, you know, interested
in the rest of the world,

00:15:28.127 --> 00:15:29.595
saw this in central China.

00:15:29.595 --> 00:15:30.729
What is this?

00:15:30.729 --> 00:15:32.364 align:start size:84% position:16%
I thought, I
believe the numbers,

00:15:32.364 --> 00:15:36.268
it's gonna be, you know,
3, 4, 5% mortality, really?

00:15:36.268 --> 00:15:38.437 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, many
millions would die.

00:15:38.437 --> 00:15:40.839
So it's not a question of
not taking COVID seriously.

00:15:40.839 --> 00:15:42.808
If you take it seriously,

00:15:42.808 --> 00:15:46.812
you want solutions
that are effective.

00:15:46.812 --> 00:15:50.082
I mean, that's how
you give the virus

00:15:50.082 --> 00:15:52.318
the respect it deserves

00:15:52.318 --> 00:15:54.620
is by responding
to it rationally.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.322 align:start size:81% position:19%
And the mask stuff
in particularly

00:15:56.322 --> 00:15:58.791
things about vaccines
too, but the mask stuff

00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:01.327
is so totally unmoored

00:16:01.327 --> 00:16:04.797 align:start size:84% position:16%
from any kind of
research data at all.

00:16:04.797 --> 00:16:06.532
In fact, there's a lot
of countervailing data

00:16:06.532 --> 00:16:09.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
that shows that it's
counterproductive and bad.

00:16:09.301 --> 00:16:10.836
We keep saying this
for like a year.

00:16:10.836 --> 00:16:12.638
We're like, well, no, there's
this new study out of Vietnam,

00:16:12.638 --> 00:16:14.106 align:start size:84% position:16%
the biggest
DataMaster ever done.

00:16:14.106 --> 00:16:17.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everyone's like, yeah,
shut up, mask denier.

00:16:17.409 --> 00:16:20.379 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I finally realized,
'cause I'm not super smart,

00:16:20.379 --> 00:16:22.448 align:start size:88% position:13%
but like, you don't care
what the evidence is.

00:16:22.448 --> 00:16:24.283
There's no interest whatsoever,

00:16:24.283 --> 00:16:26.685 align:start size:84% position:16%
masks are good, this
is what we know,

00:16:26.685 --> 00:16:27.953
this is the catechism,

00:16:27.953 --> 00:16:31.390 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I'm like, okay, this
isn't public health,

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:32.992
this is theology.

00:16:32.992 --> 00:16:34.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I don't really know
what you do with theology,

00:16:34.893 --> 00:16:36.095 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's why we don't
talk about it.

00:16:36.095 --> 00:16:37.396
Like, what, you know,
I'm in Washington,

00:16:37.396 --> 00:16:38.597
so when I was a
kid, it was like,

00:16:38.597 --> 00:16:40.099 align:start size:81% position:19%
no, you don't talk
about religion

00:16:40.099 --> 00:16:42.835
in a public setting because
it's too personal, right?

00:16:42.835 --> 00:16:45.404 align:start size:84% position:16%
Sex, religion,
politics, off limits.

00:16:45.404 --> 00:16:48.273
So I just don't really
have the tools to argue

00:16:48.273 --> 00:16:51.744 align:start size:97% position:3%
with people over religion
because my default setting is,

00:16:51.744 --> 00:16:53.479 align:start size:88% position:13%
you know, hey, everyone
has their beliefs,

00:16:53.479 --> 00:16:55.781
like, I'm very liberal that way.

00:16:55.781 --> 00:16:59.151
The problem is there's as
an evangelical religion.

00:16:59.151 --> 00:17:02.955 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, it's seventh century
Islam, it's convert or die,

00:17:02.955 --> 00:17:05.557
it's really, really
aggressive, whoa.

00:17:05.557 --> 00:17:06.959
- So what do we do with that?

00:17:06.959 --> 00:17:08.627
I mean, I've spent a lot of time

00:17:08.627 --> 00:17:10.462
when I was off the grid
thinking about just that,

00:17:10.462 --> 00:17:11.730
because I'm with you,

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:15.467
that we sort of are in a
cold civil war in that.

00:17:15.467 --> 00:17:16.769
And I don't want a civil war,

00:17:16.769 --> 00:17:18.570
obviously, and I
don't want violence

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:21.540
just as you laid out and
I want this thing to work,

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.776
but it seems to me you
have a set of people

00:17:23.776 --> 00:17:25.010 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I would include
people like us,

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:26.478 align:start size:88% position:13%
in which he's basically
live and let live,

00:17:26.478 --> 00:17:29.148 align:start size:97% position:3%
where we can talk about where
the government should be.

00:17:29.148 --> 00:17:32.718
But then we have this other
set that want everything,

00:17:32.718 --> 00:17:34.787
and they want everything from us

00:17:34.787 --> 00:17:36.755
and to tell us how
to do everything.

00:17:36.755 --> 00:17:39.124 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's not a liberal
arguing with a conservative,

00:17:39.124 --> 00:17:41.326 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's something
much more dangerous,

00:17:41.326 --> 00:17:43.862
because they are
not going to stop.

00:17:43.862 --> 00:17:45.531
So what do we do with that,

00:17:45.531 --> 00:17:48.100
those of us that
wanna live freely?

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:50.135
- You know, I don't know.

